# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# The project's Root Directory is `apps/web`, but the deploy is made from the
# repository root so that pnpm can resolve the workspace and the `catalog:`
# version pins. That means the whole tree is a candidate for upload.
#
# Without this file that came to **4.5 GB** — the pnpm store's symlink farm
# under `node_modules`, every package's `dist`, and every `.next`. Vercel
# installs dependencies itself and rebuilds from source, so none of it is
# wanted; it only makes the upload slow enough to look like a hang, which is
# exactly how it presented.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, all of it regenerated during the build.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and tooling artefacts.
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results

# Source documents that are inputs to the work, not part of the app.
*.pdf
*.docx
